1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,361
Presenter:

2
00:00:00,361 --> 00:00:04,935
This evening we’re delighted to welcome Dan Beagle,

3
00:00:04,935 --> 00:00:09,629
who’s just written a book on looking for and finding food in the

4
00:00:09,629 --> 00:00:10,030
wild.

5
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:16,360
He’s going to tell us everything we need to know about picking wild

6
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:16,410
mushrooms.

7
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:16,682
Dan:

8
00:00:16,682 --> 00:00:17,568
Thank you very much.

9
00:00:17,568 --> 00:00:22,080
Well, I need to start by talking about safety.

10
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:28,548
You really need to know what you’re doing because some mushrooms are extremely

11
00:00:28,548 --> 00:00:29,010
poisonous.

12
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:40,035
Having said that, once you know what to look for, it’s really worth doing

13
00:00:40,035 --> 00:00:50,325
for the amazing variety of mushrooms available – which you can’t get in the

14
00:00:50,325 --> 00:00:51,060
shops.

15
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:54,708
But of course, you have to be very careful and that’s why I always

16
00:00:54,708 --> 00:00:57,869
say you should never consume mushrooms picked by friends or neighbours – always remember

17
00:00:57,869 --> 00:01:00,301
that some poisonous mushrooms look very similar to edible ones

18
00:01:00,301 --> 00:01:02,490
and it’s easy for people to get confused.

19
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:09,067
The other thing to avoid is mushrooms growing beside busy roads for obvious reasons.

20
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:15,643
But nothing beats the taste of freshly picked mushrooms – don’t forget that the

21
00:01:15,643 --> 00:01:21,750
ones in the shops are often several days old and past their best.

22
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:28,349
There are certain ideas about wild mushrooms that it’s important to be aware

23
00:01:28,349 --> 00:01:28,820
of.

24
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:37,507
Don’t listen to people who tell you that it’s only OK to eat mushrooms that are pale

25
00:01:37,507 --> 00:01:40,250
or dull – this is completely untrue.

26
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:44,790
Some edible mushrooms are bright red, for example.

27
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:51,511
Personally, I prefer mushrooms cooked but it won’t do you any harm to eat

28
00:01:51,511 --> 00:01:56,440
them uncooked in salads – it’s not necessary to peel them.

29
00:01:56,440 --> 00:02:02,749
Another thing you should remember is that you can’t tell if a mushroom is

30
00:02:02,749 --> 00:02:09,057
safe to eat by its smell – some of the most deadly mushrooms have no smell

31
00:02:09,057 --> 00:02:11,160
and taste quite nice, apparently.

32
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:20,544
Finally, just because deer or squirrels eat a particular mushroom doesn’t mean that you

33
00:02:20,544 --> 00:02:21,170
can.

34
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:27,664
Of course, mushroom picking is associated with the countryside but if you haven’t got

35
00:02:27,664 --> 00:02:32,860
a car, your local park can be a great place to start.

36
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:40,074
There are usually a range of habitats where mushrooms grow, such as playing fields

37
00:02:40,074 --> 00:02:41,620
and wooded areas.

38
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:47,570
But you need to be there first thing in the morning, as there’s likely

39
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:52,330
be a lot of competition – not just from people but wildlife too.

40
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:57,470
The deer often get the best mushrooms in my local park.

41
00:02:57,470 --> 00:03:02,875
If you’re a complete beginner, I wouldn’t recommend going alone

42
00:03:02,875 --> 00:03:08,730
or relying on photos in a book, even the one I’ve written!

43
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:12,430
There are some really good phone apps for identifying mushrooms,

44
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:17,980
but you can’t always rely on getting a good signal in the middle of

45
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:18,720
a wood.

46
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:25,302
If possible, you should go with a group led by an expert – you’ll stay safe

47
00:03:25,302 --> 00:03:27,770
and learn a lot that way.

48
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:35,100
Conservation is a really important consideration and you must follow a few basic rules.

49
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:41,294
You should never pick all the mushrooms in one area – collect only enough

50
00:03:41,294 --> 00:03:43,200
for your own needs.

51
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:49,610
Be very careful that you don’t trample on young mushrooms or other plants.

52
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:55,760
And make sure you don’t pick any mushrooms that are endangered

53
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:57,810
and protected by law.

54
00:03:57,810 --> 00:04:03,739
There’s been a decline in some varieties of wild mushrooms in this part of

55
00:04:03,739 --> 00:04:04,530
the country.

56
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:09,792
Restaurants are becoming more interested in locally sourced food like wild mushrooms,

57
00:04:09,792 --> 00:04:15,931
but the biggest problem is that so many new houses have been built in

58
00:04:15,931 --> 00:04:19,000
this area in the last ten years.

59
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:25,493
And more water is being taken from rivers and reservoirs because of this,

60
00:04:25,493 --> 00:04:28,490
and mushroom habitats have been destroyed.

61
00:04:28,490 --> 00:04:33,770
Anyway, a word of advice on storing mushrooms.

62
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:38,434
Collect them in a brown paper bag and as soon as you get home,

63
00:04:38,434 --> 00:04:40,100
put them in the fridge.

64
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:43,256
They’ll be fine for a couple of days,

65
00:04:43,256 --> 00:04:48,166
but it’s best to cook them as soon as possible – after washing them

66
00:04:48,166 --> 00:04:49,920
really carefully first, of course.

67
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:55,030
So everybody knows what a mushroom tastes like, right?

68
00:04:55,030 --> 00:05:00,750
Well, you’ll be surprised by the huge variety of wild mushrooms there are.

69
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:14,513
Be adventurous!

70
00:05:14,513 --> 00:06:30,210
They’re great in so many dishes – stir fries, risottos, pasta.

71
00:06:30,210 --> 00:06:30,260
But just be aware that some people can react badly to certain varieties

72
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:30,310
so it’s a good idea not to eat huge quantities to begin with.

73
00:06:30,310 --> 00:06:30,360
OK,

74
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:30,410
so now I’m going to show you …
